    "content": "<strong>(1) Tilt defensive</strong> &mdash; staples, healthcare, utilities outperform when growth multiple compresses. <strong>(2) Pullback over Breakout</strong> &mdash; in negative-drift regime, momentum names get sold; only buy at support after a controlled retracement. <strong>(3) Position size halved</strong> &mdash; expected DD jumped from 2.9% to 4.78%; cut nominal exposure to keep portfolio-level VaR constant. <strong>(4) Gold + duration</strong> &mdash; GLD and TLT (when TLT pulls back) are the cleanest portfolio hedges. The risk-off tape doesn't necessarily mean crash &mdash; it means lower expected return and higher tail risk per unit of beta. Match the regime, don't fight it."
